-- title:
--   Type-m sublattices of Iₓ and cyclic N-subgroups of W
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$, let $X_1/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve whose group of points has no $q'$-torsion, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order (a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning, maximal among such), and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}$ of $X_1$ generated by $\kappa$-rational homomorphisms into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with range exactly $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\neq 0$ with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $m$ and $N m^{-1}$ both in the adelic box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ (the additive group generated by $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral adele), such that $\mathbb{H}\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ is a maximal order and $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$. Fix a unit $x$ of the adelic algebra, an elliptic curve $W/\kappa$, a nonzero $\kappa$-rational homomorphism $\chi:X_1\to W$ and a unit $d\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$ with $\theta_1$ of the kernel ideal set $\{\rho\circ\chi:\rho\in\mathrm{Hom}_\kappa(W,X_1)\}$ equal to the quaternion conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda_1})$. Then there is a bijection $\kappa_x$ between the lattices of the form $\mathbb{H}\cap xum\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, $u$ in the stabiliser of $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ in the adelic unit group, and the additive subgroups $C\leq W(\kappa)$ that are cyclic with $\mathrm{Nat.card}\,C=N$, such that for every such lattice $J$, every elliptic $W'/\kappa$ and every pair of $\kappa$-rational homomorphisms $\psi:W\to W'$, $\psi':W'\to W$ with $\psi'\circ\psi=N$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=N$, the equality $\theta_1$ of the kernel ideal set of $\chi$ followed by $\psi$ $=$ conjugate of $d\cdot J$ forces $\ker\psi=\kappa_x(J)$.
--
--   This is the curve side of the level-$N$ Deuring–Eichler dictionary at an end vertex: sublattices of $I_x=\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ of type $m$ (equivalently, the primitive right sublattices of reduced norm $N$ attached to an Eichler order of level $N$) are matched with the $\Gamma_0(N)$-structures, i.e. cyclic subgroups of order $N$, on the elliptic curve $W$ realising $x$, compatibly with kernel ideals of composite isogenies. It feeds the identification of the quaternionic class set with supersingular places used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd step, [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_ker).
